  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Course pages and navigation",
      "items": [
        "The hub links to four separate pages: an EEI guide, an EEI lab, a Math I guide, and a Math I lab. (index.html:68–105)",
        "Each guide links to its matching lab; each lab links back to its guide. All four pages also return to the hub. (ee1-electrostatics-guide.html:61–66; ee1-electrostatics-lab.html:61–64; math1-guide.html:61–66; math1-lab.html:61–62)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Browser state and page assets",
      "items": [
        "The EEI and Math I guide checklists use separate keys, ee1-checks and math1-checks. They restore checked items at load and save changes to this browser's localStorage. Storage errors are swallowed, so ticks may not persist when browser storage is unavailable. (js/ee1-electrostatics-guide.js:2–14; js/math1-guide.js:2–14)",
        "Every page loads Roboto fonts from Google Fonts. Only the guides load the KaTeX stylesheet; their formulas are already rendered into HTML. (index.html:11–17; ee1-electrostatics-guide.html:11–21; README.md:44–45)",
        "The guides and labs load local CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step for the pages; lab interactions run in the browser. (README.md:40–46; js/ee1-electrostatics-lab.js:205–239; js/math1-lab.js:3306–3336)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Deployment and CI",
      "items": [
        "GitHub Pages publishes the repository root from main. Every main commit starts GitHub's pages-build-deployment job. (README.md:63–66, 69)",
        "The separate Jekyll Docker workflow checks pushes and pull requests targeting main; it builds but does not publish the site. (README.md:67; .github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1–19)"
      ]
    }
  ]
